From 08f6dd429e75c4cf879a5f452e8a3832b5a6bbf0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jianying Lang <langjian@amazon.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 22:20:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] hy_v3: trn3 prefill / sparse / decode optimizations
 behind HY3_* flags

STATIC_MX prefill experts (no in-kernel reduce, weight-reload skip), top-k affinity all-gather, routing
rows padded for the NKI blockwise mapping, segmented prefill over a 64-token coarse view (bit-identical),
block-granular K/V writes, prepared sparse selection / summary updates with an NKI K-summary kernel and
flat index_select gathers, decode KVDP through a forked attention_block_tkg_kvdp with sparse selection
inside it (HY3_DECODE_KVDP_FORK; upstream HY3_DECODE_KVDP unchanged), fused decode MoE on trn3 (OCP FP8
activations), pooled output / H2D buffers (io_stable.py), prefix-cache alignment. All off by default.
Module tests: kvdp_check (8-rank, bit-exact), io_stable_check, bench_prefill_attn, bench_moe_tkg.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
