+# Hy3 fork of nkilib.core.moe.moe_tkg.gate_up_projection_mx (installed nkilib), imports made absolute.
+# Only change: for small T (decode) the MX gate/up matmul holds the T-token input STATIONARY and streams
+# the weights as the MOVING operand (512-wide I tiles), then PE-transposes the [T, 512] result into the
+# original [128_I, 4_I, T] PSUM layout. The stock loop holds 128x512 weight tiles stationary and moves only
+# T columns per matmul (LDWEIGHTS-bound at T=16: ~70 us per expert vs ~10 us of streaming).
